WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.300
How long all of this takes.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.800
An honest schedule for the whole companion, assuming you work full time and study around it.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.433
The key idea: the tracks run in parallel.

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.033
That's why the total is far less than the sum.

5
00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:16.467
There are six tracks.

6
00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.433
The three hundred eight topics, at two or three a day.

7
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:21.233
Appendices on weekends.

8
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:23.100
One scenario drill a week.

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.567
One paper a week.

10
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:27.167
A from scratch build every two to three weeks.

11
00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:30.500
And three portfolio projects, about six weeks each.

12
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.233
Here's the elapsed time for each, using the top of each range.

13
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:43.667
Topics and papers take about seven months, builds about six, portfolio about five, scenarios three, and appendices a few weeks.

14
00:00:44.867 --> 00:00:46.167
And three milestones.

15
00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:54.327
Job ready is four to five months: volumes one to seven, two portfolio projects with evals, and scenarios one to six.

16
00:00:54.327 --> 00:00:56.767
Start applying here, not at the end.

17
00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.667
The complete companion is seven to nine months.

18
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:02.986
Deep mastery takes eighteen to thirty six months.

19
00:01:02.986 --> 00:01:07.300
That's a career trajectory, not a study plan, and nobody shortcuts it.

20
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.133
Your pace changes the answer.

21
00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:15.167
With three or more hours a day, weekends included, compress it to four to six months.

22
00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:19.733
With about forty five minutes a day, it's twelve to fifteen months, still worth it.

23
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:23.133
One rule decides your real timeline.

24
00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:25.744
Never let reading run ahead of building.

25
00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:31.000
Recognition evaporates in interviews, so stop reading and build until the tracks are level.

26
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.021
Let's recap.

27
00:01:33.021 --> 00:01:34.867
Six tracks run in parallel.

28
00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.533
Job ready in about four to five months.

29
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:40.833
Complete in seven to nine, and mastery takes years.

30
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.067
And never let reading outrun building.
